<INDICATE ID = "T010251A069I03" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Control List</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "3" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "25%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "21%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "3" COLNAME = "3" COLWIDTH = "53%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1"><PTXT>Control Name</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Function</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fuel Injection Control (EFI)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Appropriate fuel injection is performed by correcting the basic injection duration, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A070"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" MOREROWS = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Ignition Timing Control (ESA)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Appropriate ignition is performed by correcting the basic ignition timing, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A071"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Knock Judgment Control (KCS)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>The presence or absence of knocking is judged based on the signal from the knock sensor.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>ECT Shift Torque Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>Reduces shift shock by retarding the ignition timing, etc. during A/T shifting.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" MOREROWS = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>ETCS-i Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>The throttle is controlled to the appropriate opening angle by correcting the throttle opening angle, calculated according to engine conditions, with signals from each sensor.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A387"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Maximum Speed Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>When the vehicle speed reaches 180km/h, the throttle valve is closed to suppress any increase in vehicle speed.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Idle Speed Control (ISC)</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "3"><PTXT>Controls the fast idle speed according to the engine coolant temperature and the idle speed after engine warm-up. Controls the idle speed by means of the fuel injection volume and throttle opening angle.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Dual VVT-i Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls the intake valve timing and exhaust valve timing to the optimum according to the engine condition.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251C001"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Electric ACIS Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Switches the effective intake pipe length of the intake manifold in 2 stages according to the engine condition.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A403"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>2-way Intake System Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Switches the intake passage in 2 stages according to the driving conditions to achieve both reduced intake noise and high output.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A373"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fuel Pump Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Turns the fuel pump ON and OFF based on the starter signal, engine speed signal, etc. Stops the fuel pump operation based on the signal from the airbag sensor.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A733"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Electric Cooling Fan Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls cooling fan ON/OFF and fan speed according to coolant temperature and air conditioner status.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A074"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Alternator Charging Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls the alternator generated voltage according to driving conditions, reducing the generation load to lower fuel consumption.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A398"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>O<SUB>2</SUB>Sensor Heater Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>According to coolant temperature and driving conditions, the O<SUB>2</SUB>Turns the sensor heater ON and OFF.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251T037"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>A/F Sensor Heater Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Turns the A/F sensor heater ON and OFF according to the coolant temperature and driving conditions.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A799"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Canister Purge Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Controls the canister purge flow volume according to the engine condition.<XREF     REFID = "S478010251A075"/>
</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>A/C Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Turns the A/C magnetic clutch ON and OFF after idle-up control to suppress idle speed fluctuations during idling. Temporarily turns the magnetic clutch OFF during acceleration, etc.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Immobiliser Control</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>If the engine control computer does not receive the engine start permission signal from the immobiliser amplifier, fuel injection and ignition control are restricted.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>CAN Communication</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>A communication IC that can exchange a large amount of information through communication lines has been adopted to communicate with other control computers.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Diagnosis</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>Using the diagnostic tool TaSCAN, accurate and detailed diagnosis, such as reading SAE-standard DTCs and data and performing Active Tests, is possible.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" VALIGN = "MIDDLE"><PTXT>Fail-safe</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY NAMEST = "2" NAMEEND = "3"><PTXT>When a malfunction occurs in a signal from any sensor, control is continued using standard values in the engine control computer, or the engine is stopped.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP></TABLE></INDICATE>
